It seems that the assertion statement is incorrect in the given code. It is currently checking if the last index is -1 or greater than or equal to 2 but the last index of the function seems to be calculated wrongly.
```cs
public static int Search(Collection c, int val)
{
    int index = 0;
    for (int i = 2; i <= c.Count; i++)
    {
        int tmp_val = c.SearchFrom(c, val, i);
        if (c.IsValid(tmp_val))
        {
            index = i;
        }
    }
    // @@@ index is either -1 or greater than or equal to 2
    return index;
}
```
My apologies for the mistake. The correct answer should be:
```cs
Debug.Assert(index == -1 || index >= 2);
